@name Japanese speaker of English
@about r and l merge into a tap, and every consonant cluster gets a vowel inserted to make syllables like ka, ri, tsu.
@rhythm syllable
@strip length
ɹ > ɾ
l > ɾ
θ > s
ð > z
v > b
æ > a
ɪ > i
ʊ > u
ə > a
ʌ > a
ɜ > a
# Consonants cannot end a syllable, so a vowel is added. The vowel depends on the consonant.
∅ > i / {ʃ,t͡ʃ,d͡ʒ} _ {C,#}
∅ > o / {t,d} _ {C,#}
∅ > u / C _ {C,#}
